# Identity import and disk reopen caller

This source-preparation crate retains the complete original166-line snapshot caller and active model fixture.
The fixed finite CLI imports11 identities, generates a twelfth package, renames a typed usage and saves real immutable snapshots.
Build the two examples with the independent integration manifest; root owns the lock, CI, offline commands and execution admission.
`import_save_reopen write ROOT KEY` must finish before a distinct `import_save_reopen read ROOT KEY` process starts.
ROOT must be an existing owned0700 canonical Samsung workspace directory; KEY is bounded ASCII, never a path.
The reader loads disk through SnapshotStore, validates both actual typing links/canonical bytes and restores a new private identity registry.
`SYSON_TEST_DIR` supplies owned test storage; `SYSON_IDENTITY_CLI` names the exact root-built example for the independent process tests.
`snapshot_identity_probe CLI ROOT` requires fresh empty storage and retains two warmups plus seven raw sample directories and child logs.
Stage includes parser/linker/commit; edit, final save, load including JSON parse and whole child/pair elapsed are separately reported.
Parse-only timing is unavailable through Importer::stage and SnapshotStore::load; fine-grained instrumentation remains OPEN.
Baseline save, validation and registry restoration are outside API clocks; process clocks include setup, validation and bounded polling/protocol overhead.
OS cache warmth is uncontrolled; min/median/max are workload observations, with external process RSS separately qualified by root.
The ordinary50–150ms and large250–1000ms ranges are contextual; no p95, native ratio, UI, durability or feature-acceptance claim follows.
Root must qualify all18 identity/all16 importer plus current caller cases, the entire donor/new tests and final fmt/Clippy/target gates.
RR13b and native/library/UI/backend restart gates remain separate; #99/#130 and human196–201 holds remain unchanged.
